# Long shell commands

## Do not

- Pipe a long command into `tail`/`head` in the same Shell call when you need exit code and full wait.
- Re-run the same command if the user says it already finished — read the terminal file.
- Use short `block_until_ms` for `docker compose up`, full `pnpm run build`, or future e2e without backgrounding.

## Patterns

### 1. Log file (preferred)

```bash
LOG=/tmp/oval-build.log
pnpm run build >"$LOG" 2>&1; ec=$?
echo "exit_code=$ec"
tail -n 40 "$LOG"
exit $ec
```

### 2. Background + terminal file

`block_until_ms: 0`, then read `terminals/<id>.txt` for `exit_code`.

## `block_until_ms` guide

| Command | Minimum |
|---------|---------|
| `pnpm run build` | 300000 (5m) |
| `docker compose up --wait` | 120000 |
| `pnpm run db:migrate` | 60000 |

Report: command, exit code, what you inspected.
